    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d609">

                <pb facs="0648" n="540" xml:id="pg540"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.60 f 2/20: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gittings</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Prague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-04-01T09:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 1, 1927—9
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 1—6:57
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>12. Department’s telegram 8, March 22, 4 p.m. Am informed that Czechoslovakia is
                    willing to reopen negotiations. Officials state that upon initiative of
                    Czechoslovak Minister at Washington, they already have prepared a draft which is
                    along the lines of the American-German treaty.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d609-f1"/>
                    Official note promised presently.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gittings</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d609-f1" n="7" xml:id="d609-f1-content">
                <p>Treaty of friendship, commerce and consular rights, signed Dec. 8, 1923; <ref
                        target="frus1923v02#pg_29"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>,
                        1923, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 29</ref>.</p>
